      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 78. Toxicity: no fetched page gives any. The ASPCA URL tried returned the plant-list index with no echinacea entry (not a confirmed absence); RHS and NC State name no toxicity (NC State only says the herbaceous parts may be steeped as a tea). Toxicity stays unknown (pets unknown). Hardiness: RHS H5. Growth: NC State 'Rapid', mapped to fast. Habit: RHS 'an upright perennial'. Drought: NC State 'drought tolerant once established', RHS genus guide 'tolerating dry soil'; high is the agent's mapping. Watering style let_top_dry and 7 days are the agent's mapping and a guess (RHS well-drained, NC State moist to occasionally dry). Size: RHS 1 to 1.5 m tall by up to 0.5 m wide, NC State 3 to 4 ft by 1 to 2 ft; 120 by 50 cm is the agent's pick. The trade hybrids in the starter-list row are less hardy than the species; these pages are about the species. Placement is from the starter-list row, not a source. Missouri Botanical Garden failed twice (certificate error). Fetched through a summarising fetch: wording not checked against the raw pages. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
